{"id":"2I","title":"Backsliding","part":{"n":2,"title":"Relationship to God"},"url":"/law/02-relationship-to-god/2i","entries":[{"id":"2I.1","text":"We should pray for help in turning to God from backsliding ways.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":80,"verses":"3"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":85,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":31,"verses":"18"},{"book":"Lamentations","chapter":5,"verses":"21"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":3,"verses":"26"}],"citation":"Psa. 80:3; Psa. 85:4; Jer. 31:18; Lam. 5:21; Acts 3:26."},{"id":"2I.2","text":"Warning not to cause or tempt others to backslide.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":28,"verses":"10"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":18,"verses":"6"}],"citation":"Prov.28:10; Matt. 18:6."},{"id":"2I.3","text":"We are commanded to turn from evil ways and to keep God's laws and statutes.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"9-10"},{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":7,"verses":"3"},{"book":"2 Kings","chapter":17,"verses":"13"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":31,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":18,"verses":"11"},{"book":"Hosea","chapter":14,"verses":"1-4"}],"citation":"Deut 30:9-10; 1 Sam. 7:3; 2 Kings 17:13; Isa. 31:6; Jer. 18:11; Hos. 14:1-4."},{"id":"2I.4","text":"Warnings of the iniquity of turning from God.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":32,"verses":"8"},{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":15,"verses":"11"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":85,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":8,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":14,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Hosea","chapter":11,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Hosea","chapter":4,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":9,"verses":"62"},{"book":"Nehemiah","chapter":9,"verses":"26"}],"citation":"Exod. 32:8; 1 Sam. 15:11; Psa. 85:8; Jer. 8:5; Jer. 14:7; Hosea 11:7; Hosea 4:16; Luke 9:62; Neh. 9:26."},{"id":"2I.5","text":"If a backsliding people shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek God's face, and turn from their wicked ways; then God will hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.","refs":[{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":7,"verses":"14"}],"citation":"2 Chron. 7:14."},{"id":"2I.6","text":"God is angered at those who turn their heart from Him.","refs":[{"book":"1 Kings","chapter":11,"verses":"9"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":78,"verses":"57,59"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":101,"verses":"3"}],"citation":"1 Kings 11:9; Psa. 78:57, 59; Psa. 101:3."},{"id":"2I.7","text":"When a righteous man turns away from his righteousness and commits iniquity, and does according to all the abominations that the wicked do, all the righteousness which he has done shall not be remembered.","refs":[{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":18,"verses":"24"}],"citation":"Ezek. 18:24."},{"id":"2I.8","text":"Backsliders are exhorted to turn again back to God.","refs":[{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":30,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":31,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":3,"verses":"12-14,22"},{"book":"Hosea","chapter":6,"verses":"1"},{"book":"1 Thessalonians","chapter":1,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"2 Chron. 30:6; Isa. 31:6; Jer. 3:12-14, 22; Hos. 6:1; 1 Thes. 1:9."},{"id":"2I.9","text":"Backsliding from God's ways causes punishment and the loss of His protection.","refs":[{"book":"Numbers","chapter":14,"verses":"43"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":14,"verses":"14"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":59,"verses":"2,14-15"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":2,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":5,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":15,"verses":"6"}],"citation":"Num. 14:43; Prov. 14:14; Isa. 59:2, 14-15; Jer. 2:19; Jer. 5:6; Jer. 15:6."},{"id":"2I.10","text":"If a people sincerely return back to God from their backsliding ways, God will bring them back from captivity, and have compassion on them.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"1-4"}],"citation":"Deut 30:1-4."},{"id":"2I.11","text":"If any will forsake the LORD and their heart turns away from Him, then His anger shall be aroused against them, and many evils and troubles shall befall them.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"17-18"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":24,"verses":"20"},{"book":"Judges","chapter":2,"verses":"12-14"},{"book":"Judges","chapter":10,"verses":"6-7"}],"citation":"Deut 30:17-18; Josh. 24:20; Judges 2:12-14; Judges 10:6-7;"},{"id":"2I.12","text":"We should endeavor to bring back those guilty of back-sliding.","refs":[{"book":"Galatians","chapter":6,"verses":"1"},{"book":"James","chapter":5,"verses":"16"}],"citation":"Gal 6:1; James 5:16."}]}